   "_dt": 1794376623.0,
   "ageDays": 0.01,
   "summary": "The National Assembly will hold a confirmation hearing for Kim Jong-chul, nominee for commissioner general of the Korean National Police Agency (KNPA), next week, officials said Wednesday. The parliamentary public administration and security committee adopted a plan to hold the hearing next Wednesday during a plenary meeting earlier in the day. The KNPA commissioner general nominee can be appointed by the president even without parliamentary consent following the confirmation hearing.",
   "summary_zh": "官员周三表示，国民议会将于下周为韩国国家警察厅（KNPA）警务总监提名人Kim Jong-chul举行确认听证会。议会公共行政与安全委员会在当天早些时候举行的全体会议上通过了于下周三举行听证会的计划。即使在确认听证会后，KNPA警务总监提名人也可由总统任命，无需获得议会同意。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The National Assembly will hold a confirmation hearing for Kim Jong-chul, nominee for commissioner general of the Korean National Police Agency (KNPA), next week, officials said Wednesday. The parliamentary public administration and security committee adopted a plan to hold the hearing next Wednesday during a plenary meeting earlier in the day. The KNPA commissioner general nominee can be appointed by the president even without parliamentary consent following the confirmation hearing. If appointed, Kim would fill a post that has remained vacant for nearly two years since former President Yoon Suk Yeol's declaration of martial law in late 2024",
