   "_dt": 1794376623.0,
   "ageDays": 0.01,
   "summary": "Unionized workers of Korea Railroad Corp. (KORAIL) said Wednesday they will launch an indefinite general strike at 9 a.m. on Dec. The Korean Railway Workers' Union announced the plan in a news conference at Seoul Station, warning the walkout will proceed unless its demands are met. In a statement, the union criticized the current promotion system for \"unfairly\" excluding field workers and said staff shortages in railway operations are directly compromising safety.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国铁道公社（KORAIL）的工会工人周三表示，将于12月上午9点启动无限期总罢工。韩国铁路工人工会在首尔站举行新闻发布会，宣布了这一计划，并警告称，除非其诉求得到满足，否则罢工将继续。工会在声明中批评现行晋升制度“不公平地”排斥一线工作人员，并称铁路运营人员短缺正直接危及安全。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Unionized workers of Korea Railroad Corp. (KORAIL) said Wednesday they will launch an indefinite general strike at 9 a.m. on Dec. 10, demanding improvements to the promotion system and the employment of more safety-related personnel. The Korean Railway Workers' Union announced the plan in a news conference at Seoul Station, warning the walkout will proceed unless its demands are met. In a statement, the union criticized the current promotion system for \"unfairly\" excluding field workers and said staff shortages in railway operations are directly compromising safety. The union plans to hold a large-scale rally at Seoul Station on Saturday, followed by a two-week safe-operation campaign and a series of regional nighttime rallies beginning Nov. 23. The walkout could disrupt KTX and conventional train services nationwide, as well as subway services in the capital area. Its impact could be greater than that of previous strikes following the integration of high-speed rail operator SR Co. into KORAIL in September",
