   "title": "Niger LGAs To Introduce Dedicated Nutrition Budget Lines In 2027",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/niger-lgas-to-introduce-dedicated-nutrition-budget-lines-in-2027/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:48:25 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794376105.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "The resolution was contained in a communiqué adopted at a two-day capacity-building retreat on sustainable nutrition financing for the executive chairmen of the 25 LGAs, organised by the Civil Society Scaling Up Nutrition in Nigeria (CS-SUNN) in partnership with the Niger State Government. According to the communiqué, the LGAs will also inaugurate and operationalise Local Government Committees on Food and Nutrition across the 25 councils by the first quarter of 2027.",
   "summary_zh": "该决议载于一份为期两天的可持续营养融资能力建设研讨会通过的公报中。研讨会面向尼日利亚25个地方政府行政区的行政主席举行，由尼日利亚民间社会推动营养规模化组织（CS-SUNN）与尼日尔州政府合作主办。公报称，这些地方政府行政区还将于2027年第一季度前，在全部25个行政委员会设立并启动地方食品与营养委员会。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The resolution was contained in a communiqué adopted at a two-day capacity-building retreat on sustainable nutrition financing for the executive chairmen of the 25 LGAs, organised by the Civil Society Scaling Up Nutrition in Nigeria (CS-SUNN) in partnership with the Niger State Government. The retreat, held in Abuja from November 5 to 6, 2026, also resolved that the local governments would move beyond budgetary approvals to ensure predictable quarterly cash releases for nutrition programmes. The chairmen further committed to developing Annual Operational Plans to guide nutrition spending and implementation, as well as strengthening accountability mechanisms to ensure that allocated funds and nutrition commodities reach intended beneficiaries. According to the communiqué, the LGAs will also inaugurate and operationalise Local Government Committees on Food and Nutrition across the 25 councils by the first quarter of 2027. The committees are expected to coordinate nutrition planning, budgeting, implementation and monitoring at the grassroots level under the leadership of the respective LGA chairmen. The retreat noted that although ₦500 million was already available in the state nutrition account, securing budgetary allocations alone was insufficient without timely releases and effective utilisation of the funds. Participants therefore called for sustained advocacy and engagement with government institutions to ensure that existing financial commitments translate into interventions that address malnutrition. They also identified the UNICEF Child Nutrition Fund’s 1:1 matching arrangement as an opportunity to mobilise additional resources for nutrition, stressing the need for timely counterpart funding by government. The communiqué further recommended capacity-building programmes for nutrition desk officers and focal persons to improve their skills in planning, budget preparation, data analysis and field monitoring. To strengthen transparency, the LGAs also resolved to collaborate with the State Committee on Food and Nutrition, CS-SUNN and community structures to track nutrition resources and prevent the diversion of commodities. Participants emphasised the need for community sensitisation and the promotion of locally produced nutritious foods, including Tom Brown, to encourage demand for maternal, infant and young child feeding services. The retreat observed that nutrition interventions were often carried out on an ad hoc basis in many LGAs due to the absence of dedicated budget lines, making structured planning and predictable financing necessary for sustainable results. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates → Join Our WhatsApp Channel --> --> Patience Ivie Ihejirika Patience Ivie Ihejirika is an award-winning journalist with Leadership Newspaper, specialising in health reporting. She is known for in-depth coverage, compelling human-interest stories, and well-researched special reports that have distinguished her in the field",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
