   "title": "Korea to extend fuel tax cuts through January to ease price burdens",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/economy/policy/20261111/korea-to-extend-fuel-tax-cuts-through-january-to-ease-price-burdens",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:47:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1794365223.0,
   "ageDays": 0.14,
   "summary": "Korea will extend its fuel tax cuts by another two months through January to ease the financial burden on the public amid lingering uncertainty in the Middle East, the finance ministry said Wednesday. The Ministry of Finance and Economy said the decision was made at a meeting of economy-related ministers chaired by Finance Minister Lee Hyoung-il, taking into account the need to ease the burden on households and the government's capacity to respond to future price volatility.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国财政部周三表示，韩国将在1月前再延长两个月的燃油税减免措施，以在中东持续存在不确定性的情况下减轻公众的经济负担。经济财政部长官李亨一致主持经济相关部长会议，并在作决定时考虑了减轻家庭负担以及政府应对未来价格波动能力的需要。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Korea will extend its fuel tax cuts by another two months through January to ease the financial burden on the public amid lingering uncertainty in the Middle East, the finance ministry said Wednesday. The Ministry of Finance and Economy said the decision was made at a meeting of economy-related ministers chaired by Finance Minister Lee Hyoung-il, taking into account the need to ease the burden on households and the government's capacity to respond to future price volatility. Under the measure, the current tax cuts of 15 percent on gasoline and 25 percent on diesel and butane, originally set to expire at the end of this month, will remain in place through the end of January. The ministry said the larger tax cuts on diesel and butane reflect the importance of diesel to industrial and logistics operations and the widespread use of butane as fuel for small trucks",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
