   "summary": "Foreign Minister Cho Hyun met with U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio in France on Tuesday to discuss North Korea and bilateral issues, Seoul's foreign ministry said. Cho held a pull-aside meeting with Rubio on the sidelines of a Group of Seven (G7) foreign ministers' meeting and \"exchanged views on overall bilateral relations, high-level exchanges and North Korea-related issues,\" the ministry said, without disclosing other details.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国外交部长赵显周二在法国会见了美国国务卿马尔科·鲁比奥，讨论朝鲜半岛及双边事务。韩国外交部表示，在七国集团（G7）外长会议期间，赵显与鲁比奥另行简短会晤，并“就双边关系整体情况、高层交流以及与朝鲜有关的问题交换了意见”，但未披露其他细节。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Foreign Minister Cho Hyun met with U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio in France on Tuesday to discuss North Korea and bilateral issues, Seoul's foreign ministry said. Cho held a pull-aside meeting with Rubio on the sidelines of a Group of Seven (G7) foreign ministers' meeting and \"exchanged views on overall bilateral relations, high-level exchanges and North Korea-related issues,\" the ministry said, without disclosing other details. The meeting came as the South Korean Cabinet approved a bill earlier in the day seeking parliamentary consent for the government's plan to expand the operational scope of its anti-piracy Cheonghae unit from waters off the Somali coast to areas closer to the Strait of Hormuz. U.S. President Donald Trump has called on South Korea and other countries to help secure the vital waterway, which remains effectively blocked amid the U.S.-Iran war",
