   "title": "Lee says Korea will continue cooperation with US administration",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/politics/20261110/lee-says-will-continue-cooperation-with-us-administration-seek-bipartisan-support-in-congress",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Tue, 10 Nov 2026 05:47:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1794289623.0,
   "ageDays": 1.02,
   "summary": "President Lee Jae Myung said Tuesday that Korea will continue to closely cooperate with the U.S. administration following the recent U.S. midterm elections, while also seeking to expand bipartisan support in Congress for issues related to the country and the alliance.",
   "summary_zh": "李在明总统周二表示，在美国近期中期选举结束后，韩国将继续与美国政府密切合作，同时争取扩大美国国会对涉及韩国及韩美同盟议题的两党支持。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "President Lee Jae Myung said Tuesday that Korea will continue to closely cooperate with the U.S. administration following the recent U.S. midterm elections, while also seeking to expand bipartisan support in Congress for issues related to the country and the alliance. Lee made the remarks at a Cabinet meeting after the opposition Democratic Party in the United States won control of both the Senate and the House of Representatives in last week's midterm elections. \"After the U.S. midterm elections, many changes are expected to take place in the external environment,\" the Korean president said, instructing officials to prepare thoroughly for any possible changes. \"Utmost attention should be paid to minimizing negative effects from external uncertainties on the domestic economy.\" \"More important than anything would be strengthening and expanding the foundation for cooperation and trust between the two countries from the mutually beneficial perspective,\" Lee added, calling for efforts to ensure the implementation of bilateral diplomatic and security agreements. The president, in particular, stressed the importance of sufficiently protecting national interests and investments of Korean firms. \"To that end, (Korea) would need to continue close cooperation with the U.S. administration, while, at the same time, establishing a bipartisan foundation for cooperation in Congress and expanding the scope of communication with the state governments and the economic sector,\" the president noted. He also stressed the importance of consistency and flexibility amid global uncertainties, pledging to focus on diplomacy that prioritizes national interests and policies benefiting the people",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "kr"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol",
    "eco"
   ],
   "tier": 2,
   "actor": "美国",
   "alsoUS": false,
