   "title": "PHOTOS: NEMA receives six Nigerian returnees from US",
   "url": "https://punchng.com/photos-nema-receives-six-nigerian-returnees-from-us/",
   "domain": "punchng.com",
   "source": "Punch（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Sun, 08 Nov 2026 13:25:15 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794144315.0,
   "ageDays": 2.7,
   "summary": "The National Emergency Management Agency has received six Nigerian returnees from the United States at the Murtala Muhammed International Airport, Lagos State. NEMA disclosed this in a statement posted on its X handle on Sunday, saying the returnees arrived at the airport’s Cargo Terminal on November 4, 2026.",
   "summary_zh": "国家紧急事务管理局在拉各斯州穆尔塔拉·穆罕默德国际机场接收了6名从美国返回的尼日利亚人。国家紧急事务管理局周日在其X账号发布的声明中透露，这些归国人员于2026年11月4日抵达机场货运航站楼。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The National Emergency Management Agency has received six Nigerian returnees from the United States at the Murtala Muhammed International Airport, Lagos State. NEMA disclosed this in a statement posted on its X handle on Sunday, saying the returnees arrived at the airport’s Cargo Terminal on November 4, 2026. The agency said the reception exercise was conducted through its Lagos Operations Office in collaboration with the United States Consulate, the Federal Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the Nigeria Immigration Service and ExecuJet. “The returnees arrived at approximately 10:13 p.m. aboard a Beechcraft 1900 aircraft with registration number N62FF. The group comprised five males and one female, all adults. “Upon arrival, officers of the Nigeria Immigration Service conducted the necessary immigration documentation and profiling to ensure proper identification, record-keeping and a smooth arrival process. “NEMA coordinated the reception in collaboration with the relevant agencies, while necessary reception and post-arrival support services were provided to facilitate the returnees’ transition following their arrival in the country,” the statement said. The agency did not state the circumstances under which the six returned, whether they were deported or returned of their own free will. US, under President Donald Trump, intensified US immigration enforcement, which has prioritized stricter rules, accelerated removals of individuals without legal status, and targeted those with criminal records through initiatives such as the “worst of the worst” lists and West Africa Operations Watch. Nigeria has featured prominently in these efforts, with the US Department of Homeland Security publishing multiple lists of Nigerian nationals identified for deportation in 2026, often linked to offences including fraud and other violations. Meanwhile, NEMA said the returning exercise reflected the Federal Government’s efforts to ensure the safe, orderly and dignified return of Nigerian citizens through coordinated engagement among relevant agencies and partners. Saheed Oyelakin Saheed is a journalist at Punch Newspapers with over two years of experience covering metro, technology, sports, politics, and human-interest stories. He focuses on producing clear, engaging reports across diverse beats. Saheed’s work reflects hands-on newsroom experience and a commitment to accurate and balanced journalism",
